Considering : a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human degree, dignity and honor and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence and discrimination as a form of respect, protection and enforcement of Human Rights, particularly the basic rights of women and children, so that it is necessary to regulate the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children in Pekalongan Regency;

b. that based on the consideration as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to stipulate a Regional Regulation of Pekalongan Regency concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the Constitution of the State of the Republic of Indonesia of 1945;

2. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Province of Central Java;

